# --- Generated native projects -----------------------------------------------
# `expo prebuild` regenerates both from app.config.ts. Measured, not guessed:
#
#   ios/      4.7 GB — 3.4 GB of build output and 1.2 GB of CocoaPods
#   android/  264 KB — checked in, see below
#
# `ios/` stays out because of that 4.7 GB, essentially all of it build artefacts
# rather than source, and because it is unusable on a PC anyway.
#
# `android/` IS committed. It is tiny, and Expo generates its own
# `android/.gitignore` covering `build/`, `.gradle`, `local.properties`, `.cxx/`
# and `*.jsbundle` — so the build output and the machine-specific SDK path stay
# out on their own, and only source is tracked. Committing it makes the repo
# plug-and-play for a Windows developer, who would otherwise have to prebuild
# before the project would open at all.
#
# The trade: `android/` no longer regenerates automatically. If `app.config.ts`
# changes anything native — permissions, package id, icons — re-run
# `npx expo prebuild --platform android` and commit the result.
ios/

# Contains the linked Supabase project reference.
supabase/.temp/

.DS_Store
